@nsobid-6C4BC35D955FABDEF98616FA93F38FAF49B5FE48

# Clubhouse Games 51 Worldwide Classics 2.0.1 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables both of the game's FXAA passes.
//
// The first is folded into nd::NdRender's tonemapping: the tonemap pass
// (sub_71002F9C24) picks one of ten shader programs,
// tonemap_{linear,filmic,ut2,reinhard,gt} (10-14) or the same five with FXAA
// folded in, posteffect_fxaa_tonemap_* (15-19). The choice comes from the post
// effect's fxaa_enable flag (sub_71002BF098), which is also forced on whenever
// the console is docked. Taking the plain tonemap program keeps tonemapping
// identical and only drops the FXAA blur.
//
// The second is the Bezel PostFx effect named "FXAA" (pfx_fxaa shader,
// PostFxFxaa parameters). The post chain asks each effect whether it is enabled
// for the viewport before drawing it; the FXAA effect's answer (sub_7100766978)
// is now always false, so the chain skips it as it does when the effect's
// parameters turn it off.

@enabled
002F9DD8 E103082A   // MOV W1,W8 = plain tonemap program (was CSEL W1,W9,W8,NE)
00766978 00008052   // MOV W0,#0: PostFx FXAA is never enabled (was STP X29,X30,[SP,#-0x20]!)
0076697C C0035FD6   // RET
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Clubhouse Games 51 Worldwide Classics
// 2.0.1 (NdCube Bezel engine + nd::NdRender, NVN). The retail build keeps only
// a partial symbol table; every site was located by structure and byte-verified
// against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
